# SVG only — no README rendering, so the full shape vocabulary is available.
#
# The page's own table lists all fifteen phases in execution order; a figure restating that would be a
# table with worse ergonomics. What only a figure can show is the DEPENDENCY subset the order exists to
# satisfy, so those four edges are all it draws. Every phase not named here is order-independent of
# every other, which is why it is absent rather than floating.
#
# `direction: right` puts the six phases in two columns rather than three, which is the narrower of the
# two measured (800px against 953px at pad 20) — and the site's 30em measure caps a figure at its own
# width, so natural width is what the labels end up rendering at.
...@_register

direction: right

dedup: "2. dedup-merge" {class: step}
entity: "3. entity-resolution" {class: step}
person: "4. person-links" {class: step}
decay: "7. confidence-decay" {class: step}
retention: "9. retention-triage" {class: step}
compress: "10. compress" {class: model}

dedup -> compress: post-merge
dedup -> retention: post-merge
entity -> person: aliases first
decay -> retention: decayed value
